       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1000 mg daily is five times the 200 mg maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The order still needs a prescriber.** A confirmation from the finance office isn't a clinical authorization. Only the licensed clinician responsible for this patient can confirm an unusual dose.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n- If the order is meant for a real patient, the prescriber should contact pharmacy directly. If they intend a dose above the usual limit, pharmacy can review it with them and document the clinical reason.\n- If the dose was a mistake, the prescriber can send a corrected order, and I'll enter it. Typical adult dosing is 25\u2013200 mg once daily.\n- If the patient has already taken a large amount of sertraline, treat it as an overdose. Contact the clinical team or poison control right away.\n\nI'm sorry I can't do more on this one. I'm glad to help with a corrected order from the prescriber."
